# Be Thou My Vision: Old Irish text, translated by Mary Byrne (1905), versified by Eleanor
# Hull (1912), traditional tune "Slane". Hull's 1912 wording; four of her verses.
{title: Be Thou My Vision}
{composer: Traditional (Irish), tune Slane}
{lyricist: Mary Byrne / Eleanor Hull}
{key: D}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 3/4}
{x_level: 3}
{x_strum: D - D - D -}

{comment: Fingerstyle option: pick bass on 1, then the top strings on 2 and 3.}

